values ('e7f8a9b0-1c2d-4e32-9b12-2f3a4b5c6d52', 'asian-religions', 'Asian Religions', 'Students begin by learning how scholars define religion, Asia, tradition, scripture, ritual, philosophy, and lived practice without flattening diverse communities into a single essence. The course studies Vedic sacrifice and social order, the philosophical and soteriological vocabulary of Upanishadic and classical thought, plural Hindu practice, early Buddhism and later Mahayana and Vajrayana traditions, Jain and Sikh ethics, Chinese religious worlds, Daoism, Confucianism, East Asian Buddhism, Japanese traditions, Southeast Asian landscapes, and modern diaspora, reform, and comparative interpretation.');

