nd monastic activism"}], "description": "Students learn major Buddhist worlds of mainland Southeast Asia."}, {"id": "1eb51ba5-e2c4-4da3-b426-5a25d6e390f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hindu-Buddhist pasts", "children": [{"id": "04a1e224-837c-4cc6-a5c2-6c29bb3c43e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Angkor, Borobudur, Prambanan, epics, kingship, Sanskrit cosmopolis, and local adaptation"}, {"id": "a06a0622-935b-40cb-bdd8-57d7fcba8c17", "type": "concept", "title": "Ritual power, temples, inscriptions, and art"}, {"id": "a5e57e58-1dc0-4daf-894c-ed918a34f2be", "type": "concept", "title": "Heritage, tourism, and national memory"}], "description": "The point is to see deep premodern connections across the region."}, {"id": "91544b1e-1531-4b00-987f-2a2236cfc26b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plural religious landscapes", "children": [{"id": "2803c75e-78e5-4c9e-9e4b-c450d9371299", "type": "concept", "title": "Islam, Christianity, local spirits, ancestor practices, Chinese religion, Hindu communities, and new movements"}, {"id": "b3e77aa8-0a4f-4882-bb86-4e87b1d0671a", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonialism, mission, reform, and nation-state law"}, {"id": "62ef66d5-f465-4981-80f6-4f0ac7bc77cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Minority religion and interreligious conflict/coexistence"}], "description": "Students examine interaction among multiple traditions."}]}, {"id": "92333314-1804-437f-adad-facc8c655d34", "type": "topic", "title": "Modern Transformations: Diaspora, Colonialism, Nationalism, Gender, Ecology, Digital Religion, and Global Flows", "description": "This module studies how Asian religions adapt in modern states, diasporas, media systems, interfaith spaces, reform movements, and global politics.", "children": [{"id": "3b98ad2a-b18d-4dfc-ad13-8272e1f259d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Colonial and nationalist reform", "children": [{"id": "3f2ed24a-ae1a-4be8-9d4b-16f6fd830aba", "type": "concept", "title": "Orientalism, census, reform, revival, print, education, law,